Origin: upstream, https://git.ffmpeg.org/gitweb/ffmpeg.git/commit/4faafb7e8c2585d3e342343be0823e6e14e2bf6c
From 4faafb7e8c2585d3e342343be0823e6e14e2bf6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:59:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 26/48] cbs_h264, cbs_h265: read and write the multiview and
 depth information SEI messages

Every multiview and depth information SEI message of H.264 (multiview
scene information, multiview acquisition information, multiview view
position, depth representation information, 3D reference displays
information, depth timing, depth sampling information, constrained depth
parameter set identifier, alternative depth information; Annexes G, H
and I) and H.265 (depth representation information, multiview scene
information, multiview acquisition information, multiview view position,
alternative depth information; Annexes G and I), with the elements they
share in cbs_multiview_template.c: the camera and display parameters,
whose mantissas are up to 64 bits long, the depth representation
elements, the cameras and the global view and depth information.

The data after a reserved depth_representation_type is kept as payload
extension data. A depth timing message with per_view_depth_timing_flag
holds one offset for each of the NumDepthViews depth views of the MVCD
sequence parameter set, which CBS does not read, so the offsets the
payload holds are read. H.265 multiview acquisition information is read
outside of a scalable nesting message, for one camera (G.14.3.6).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
